{
 "format": "estate-crucible-horror/1",
 "id": "H-0095",
 "title": "A COBOL RERUN clause in I-O-CONTROL names a checkpoint data set that no SELECT assigns",
 "category": "cobol",
 "issue": 4891,
 "shapes": [
  "BDLD cobol/BDLDCKP.cbl: I-O-CONTROL. RERUN ON SYSCKPT EVERY 1000 RECORDS OF TRAN-FILE",
  "BDLD jcl/BDLDCKJ.jcl CKP010: SYSCKPT DD DSN=PROD.BDLD.CHKPT, the checkpoint data set, beside TRANIN, the file's own DD"
 ],
 "asserts": "The SELECT of TRAN-FILE is one file_control fact assigned to TRANIN and carrying rerun {assign SYSCKPT, every 1000}. SYSCKPT is the checkpoint file's assignment-name, not a file of the program: no file_control fact for it. I-O-CONTROL is a paragraph of the ENVIRONMENT DIVISION, not a unit.",
 "citations": [
  {
   "doc": "Enterprise COBOL for z/OS 6.3 Language Reference (SC27-8713-02)",
   "section": "RERUN clause",
   "url": "https://publibfp.dhe.ibm.com/epubs/pdf/igy6lr30.pdf",
   "quote": "The RERUN clause specifies that checkpoint records are to be taken."
  },
  {
   "doc": "Enterprise COBOL for z/OS 6.3 Language Reference (SC27-8713-02)",
   "section": "RERUN clause > assignment-name-1",
   "url": "https://publibfp.dhe.ibm.com/epubs/pdf/igy6lr30.pdf",
   "quote": "It must not be the same assignment-name as that specified in any ASSIGN clause throughout the entire program, including contained and containing programs."
  },
  {
   "doc": "Enterprise COBOL for z/OS 6.3 Language Reference (SC27-8713-02)",
   "section": "RERUN clause > EVERY integer-1 RECORDS",
   "url": "https://publibfp.dhe.ibm.com/epubs/pdf/igy6lr30.pdf",
   "quote": "A checkpoint record is to be written for every integer-1 records in file-name-1 that are processed."
  }
 ],
